This program finds prime numbers.

A number is prime when it is at least 2 and none of the numbers from 2 up to
its square root divide it evenly.
    1. Define a function is_prime that takes a whole number n and gives back
       true or false.
    2. In is_prime: if n is less than 2, give back false.
    3. In is_prime: for every divisor starting at 2, while the divisor times
       itself is at most n, give back false if n divided by the divisor leaves
       no remainder.
    4. In is_prime: otherwise give back true.
    Assumption: Checking divisors while their square is at most n is the same as
        checking up to the square root.

Collect every prime below 50 into a list. Print the list, and then print how
many primes were found.
    1. Make an empty list of whole numbers named primes.
    2. For every whole number n from 2 to 49, add n to the end of primes if
       is_prime of n is true.
    3. Print primes.
    4. Print "Found", the number of items in primes, and "primes".
    Assumption: "Below 50" means up to and including 49.
    Assumption: The list is printed in the form [2, 3, 5].

Finally tell whether 97 is prime.
    1. If is_prime of 97 is true, print "97 is prime"; otherwise print "97 is
       not prime".
